  <h2>What PetPomo is</h2>
  <p>
    PetPomo is a free productivity timer with a virtual pet, running entirely in your browser. It is a game and a
    focus aid. It is not medical, psychological or professional advice of any kind.
  </p>

  <h2>Your save file is yours to look after</h2>
  <p>
    Progress is stored in your browser. Clearing site data, switching browsers or using private browsing will lose
    it. Cloud sync is offered as a convenience and is not a backup service — we make no promise that a synced save
    will still be there tomorrow. Settings has an export button; use it if your progress matters to you.
  </p>

  <h2>Accounts</h2>
  <p>
    An account is optional — the game plays in full without one. If you create one, with an email and password or with
    Continue with Google, a few things follow:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Give accurate details, and keep your password to yourself. What happens under your account is your responsibility.</li>
    <li>One person, one account; do not impersonate someone else or sign up on their behalf.</li>
    <li>Tell us through <a href="/contact">the contact page</a> if you think someone else is using your account.</li>
    <li>We may suspend or close an account that is used for abuse, or that breaks these terms.</li>
    <li>You can delete your account at any time from the contact page; doing so removes it and any save attached to it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Attack, overload or attempt to break into the service or its infrastructure.</li>
